{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013z9uHu2U2ruo8K74evknhf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PENILAIAN PRESTASI / PERFORMANCE ASSESSMENT\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/PA\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU MUDA / LIGHT BLUE (Ocean Blue)\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance (G452-010-3:2023-C01)\n9\t\n10\t| Field | Detail |\n11\t|-------|--------|\n12\t| Duration | 2 hours 30 minutes |\n13\t| Total Marks | 100 |\n14\t| Passing Mark | 60% (60 marks) |\n15\t| Work Activities Covered | WA1, WA2, WA3 |\n16\t\n17\t---\n18\t\n19\t## Instructions to Candidates\n20\t\n21\t1. This performance assessment consists of THREE (3) practical tasks\n22\t2. Complete ALL tasks within the allocated time\n23\t3. Follow all safety procedures — failure to comply with critical safety requirements results in automatic failure\n24\t4. You will be assessed on PROCESS, OUTPUT, ATTITUDE, SAFETY, and ENVIRONMENT\n25\t5. A training BEV and fully equipped work bay will be provided\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## TASK 1: BEV Scheduled Maintenance Workplace Preparation (25 marks)\n30\t**Time Allocation: 30 minutes**\n31\t**Reference: WA1 — KK(1/3)**\n32\t\n33\tPrepare a BEV maintenance work bay for a scheduled maintenance service. You must:\n34\t\n35\t1. Inspect and don all required PPE correctly (5 marks)\n36\t2. Set up the work bay with barrier stanchions and HV signage (4 marks)\n37\t3. Verify all safety equipment: fire extinguisher (Class D), electric rescue hook, safety box (4 marks)\n38\t4. Inspect insulated tools and common tools; remove any defective items (4 marks)\n39\t5. Complete a Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) form for BEV scheduled maintenance (5 marks)\n40\t6. Conduct a toolbox talk covering task overview, hazards, PPE, and emergency procedures (3 marks)\n41\t\n42\t---\n43\t\n44\t## TASK 2: BEV Health Check Activities (40 marks)\n45\t**Time Allocation: 60 minutes**\n46\t**Reference: WA2 — KK(2/3)**\n47\t\n48\tPerform a complete BEV health check on the provided training vehicle. You must:\n49\t\n50\t1. Verify vehicle information: registration, VIN, mileage (4 marks)\n51\t2. Perform a systematic exterior walk-around inspection (6 marks)\n52\t3. Perform an interior systems check (4 marks)\n53\t4. Connect the diagnostic scan tool and perform a full system scan (5 marks)\n54\t5. Read and record all fault codes with freeze frame data (5 marks)\n55\t6. Perform BEV-specific system checks: battery SOC/SOH, cell voltages, insulation resistance, thermal management, charging status (8 marks)\n56\t7. Perform component active tests as supported by the diagnostic tool (3 marks)\n57\t8. Prepare and submit a complete BEV health check report with condition ratings and recommendations (5 marks)\n58\t\n59\t---\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c637cc40-8152-404a-aa5d-36736366ea90","uuid":"42a2a631-e3b6-4807-857a-bd28999f608b","timestamp":"2026-04-17T09:32:32.635Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/noss-to-wim/bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/PA.md","content":"# PENILAIAN PRESTASI / PERFORMANCE ASSESSMENT\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/PA\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU MUDA / LIGHT BLUE (Ocean Blue)\n\n---\n\n## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance (G452-010-3:2023-C01)\n\n| Field | Detail |\n|-------|--------|\n| Duration | 2 hours 30 minutes |\n| Total Marks | 100 |\n| Passing Mark | 60% (60 marks) |\n| Work Activities Covered | WA1, WA2, WA3 |\n\n---\n\n## Instructions to Candidates\n\n1. This performance assessment consists of THREE (3) practical tasks\n2. Complete ALL tasks within the allocated time\n3. Follow all safety procedures — failure to comply with critical safety requirements results in automatic failure\n4. You will be assessed on PROCESS, OUTPUT, ATTITUDE, SAFETY, and ENVIRONMENT\n5. A training BEV and fully equipped work bay will be provided\n\n---\n\n## TASK 1: BEV Scheduled Maintenance Workplace Preparation (25 marks)\n**Time Allocation: 30 minutes**\n**Reference: WA1 — KK(1/3)**\n\nPrepare a BEV maintenance work bay for a scheduled maintenance service. You must:\n\n1. Inspect and don all required PPE correctly (5 marks)\n2. Set up the work bay with barrier stanchions and HV signage (4 marks)\n3. Verify all safety equipment: fire extinguisher (Class D), electric rescue hook, safety box (4 marks)\n4. Inspect insulated tools and common tools; remove any defective items (4 marks)\n5. Complete a Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) form for BEV scheduled maintenance (5 marks)\n6. Conduct a toolbox talk covering task overview, hazards, PPE, and emergency procedures (3 marks)\n\n---\n\n## TASK 2: BEV Health Check Activities (40 marks)\n**Time Allocation: 60 minutes**\n**Reference: WA2 — KK(2/3)**\n\nPerform a complete BEV health check on the provided training vehicle. You must:\n\n1. Verify vehicle information: registration, VIN, mileage (4 marks)\n2. Perform a systematic exterior walk-around inspection (6 marks)\n3. Perform an interior systems check (4 marks)\n4. Connect the diagnostic scan tool and perform a full system scan (5 marks)\n5. Read and record all fault codes with freeze frame data (5 marks)\n6. Perform BEV-specific system checks: battery SOC/SOH, cell voltages, insulation resistance, thermal management, charging status (8 marks)\n7. Perform component active tests as supported by the diagnostic tool (3 marks)\n8. Prepare and submit a complete BEV health check report with condition ratings and recommendations (5 marks)\n\n---\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":149}}}
