{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ks8gVpRsWz5TdW7bCLP6X4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"tests/test_hv_component_index.py — Tests for BEV HV Component Indexer (US-038)\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\timport importlib.util\n6\timport json\n7\timport sys\n8\tfrom pathlib import Path\n9\t\n10\timport pytest\n11\t\n12\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n13\t# Load the module under test without requiring a package __init__.py\n14\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n15\t_SCRIPTS = Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"scripts\"\n16\t_INDEX_PATH = (\n17\t    Path(__file__).parent.parent\n18\t    / \"bev-diagnostic-rectification\"\n19\t    / \"_reference\"\n20\t    / \"hv-component-index.json\"\n21\t)\n22\t\n23\tspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\n24\t    \"index_hv_components\", _SCRIPTS / \"index_hv_components.py\"\n25\t)\n26\tassert spec and spec.loader\n27\t_mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n28\tsys.modules[\"index_hv_components\"] = _mod\n29\tspec.loader.exec_module(_mod)  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n30\t\n31\textract_components = _mod.extract_components\n32\tvalidate_safety_fields = _mod.validate_safety_fields\n33\tscan_kp_files = _mod.scan_kp_files\n34\tbuild_index = _mod.build_index\n35\tgenerate_validation_report = _mod.generate_validation_report\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n39\t# 1. JSON index file tests\n40\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n41\t\n42\t\n43\tclass TestHvComponentIndexFile:\n44\t    def test_index_file_exists(self) -> None:\n45\t        assert _INDEX_PATH.exists(), f\"Index file not found: {_INDEX_PATH}\"\n46\t\n47\t    def test_index_has_at_least_15_components(self) -> None:\n48\t        data = json.loads(_INDEX_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n49\t        assert len(data[\"components\"]) >= 15, (\n50\t            f\"Expected >=15 components, got {len(data['components'])}\"\n51\t        )\n52\t\n53\t    def test_every_component_has_required_fields(self) -> None:\n54\t        data = json.loads(_INDEX_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n55\t        required = {\"id\", \"name_en\", \"name_bm\", \"function\", \"voltage_range\", \"safety_standard\", \"cus_referenced\"}\n56\t        for comp in data[\"components\"]:\n57\t            missing = required - comp.keys()\n58\t            assert not missing, f\"Component {comp.get('id','?')} missing fields: {missing}\"\n59\t\n60\t    def test_every_component_has_nonempty_voltage_and_safety(self) -> None:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c637cc40-8152-404a-aa5d-36736366ea90","uuid":"3b983ff0-d49e-468f-a07a-079c54815397","timestamp":"2026-04-17T09:32:36.710Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/noss-to-wim/tests/test_hv_component_index.py","content":"\"\"\"tests/test_hv_component_index.py — Tests for BEV HV Component Indexer (US-038)\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Load the module under test without requiring a package __init__.py\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n_SCRIPTS = Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"scripts\"\n_INDEX_PATH = (\n    Path(__file__).parent.parent\n    / \"bev-diagnostic-rectification\"\n    / \"_reference\"\n    / \"hv-component-index.json\"\n)\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\n    \"index_hv_components\", _SCRIPTS / \"index_hv_components.py\"\n)\nassert spec and spec.loader\n_mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nsys.modules[\"index_hv_components\"] = _mod\nspec.loader.exec_module(_mod)  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n\nextract_components = _mod.extract_components\nvalidate_safety_fields = _mod.validate_safety_fields\nscan_kp_files = _mod.scan_kp_files\nbuild_index = _mod.build_index\ngenerate_validation_report = _mod.generate_validation_report\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. JSON index file tests\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass TestHvComponentIndexFile:\n    def test_index_file_exists(self) -> None:\n        assert _INDEX_PATH.exists(), f\"Index file not found: {_INDEX_PATH}\"\n\n    def test_index_has_at_least_15_components(self) -> None:\n        data = json.loads(_INDEX_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        assert len(data[\"components\"]) >= 15, (\n            f\"Expected >=15 components, got {len(data['components'])}\"\n        )\n\n    def test_every_component_has_required_fields(self) -> None:\n        data = json.loads(_INDEX_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        required = {\"id\", \"name_en\", \"name_bm\", \"function\", \"voltage_range\", \"safety_standard\", \"cus_referenced\"}\n        for comp in data[\"components\"]:\n            missing = required - comp.keys()\n            assert not missing, f\"Component {comp.get('id','?')} missing fields: {missing}\"\n\n    def test_every_component_has_nonempty_voltage_and_safety(self) -> None:","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":206}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01K5N2m5u6KNJNd9bRATRQuk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the patterns. Let me now write the implementation.\n\nFor `_tools/assessment-time-validator.py`, I need to:\n1. Parse KA/PA markdown files\n2. Detect question types (multiple choice, essay/short answer, scenario, practical)\n3. Estimate time per question type\n4. Calculate total assessment duration\n5. Generate CSV report by CU\n6. Flag assessments exceeding 110% of limit\n\nFor the question type detection:\n- Multiple choice: `- A.`, `- B.`, `- C.`, `- D.` pattern (MCQ), or `**A[0-9].` pattern = 2 min\n\n\n- Short answer / essay: Section B questions (structured short answer) = 6 min average\n- Scenario / structured: Section C questions (scenario-based) = 9 min average\n- Practical tasks: PA tasks = 15 min each\n\nThe KA recommended limit is 60 min, PA recommended limit is 90 min. Looking at BEV C01/KA.md as an example: Section A has 10 MCQ totaling 20 minutes, Section B has 5 short answer questions at 30 minutes, and Section C has 3 scenario questions that I need to calculate the time for.\n\nNow I'm seeing the PA tasks are structured differently than individual questions—each task has multiple subtasks and takes significantly longer. Task 1 is 30 minutes with 6 subtasks, Task 2 is 60 minutes, and I need to look at how the timing breaks down across these larger practical components. I see the issue—I shouldn't be reading the existing time allocations in the files, but rather estimating based on question count. Let me set up a proper validator that counts each question type and applies standard time estimates: 2 minutes for MCQs, 6 minutes for short answers, 9 minutes for scenario questions, and 15 minutes for practical tasks, then flags any assessment that exceeds the 90-minute limit.\n\nWriting the validator script... Writing the assessment parser... I'm parsing through the file line by line to detect section headers for KA files, identifying whether we're in Section A, B, C, or another section to properly categorize the questions.\n\nContinuing with the pattern matching...\n\nNow I'm calculating the total exam time by multiplying the count of each question type by its time allocation, then summing them together. After that, I'm setting up a function to scan through all assessment files in the project, iterating through both KA and PA document types and processing each one according to its limits.\n\nFor each assessment file found, I'm extracting the subject and course unit from the file path, skipping any files in archive or reference directories. Then I'm calculating the duration and comparing it against the time limit to flag any assessments that exceed 110% of the allowed time, storing all the relevant metrics in a results row.\n\nWriting the report generation... Writing the test file... Writing test cases... Now I'm setting up test cases for the assessment duration calculator, defining sample data for performance assessments with timed tasks and then writing unit tests to verify that the function correctly parses and counts different question types from markdown files. Writing test cases... Writing test cases... I'm finishing up the test and then moving on to write both files. The main module should be around 110 lines and the test file about 140 lines, which keeps me under the 350-line budget even accounting for formatting expansion. Now I need to verify the regex patterns for counting question types in Section A.\n\nLooking at the markdown format, questions start with `**A1.**`, `**A2.**` and so on, so I'll use a pattern that matches the bold markers at the beginning of a line followed by the section letter and number.\n\nI'm refining the section detection logic to track which section we're in as we parse through the file, checking for section headers and then identifying questions within each section using the bold-formatted pattern. Finishing the question counting logic for each section type, then realizing I should handle non-BEV subjects and Chinese files differently—but the acceptance criteria focuses on English sections, so the regex approach works fine. I'm thinking about adding a fallback to count any bold-numbered questions if no sections are detected, and considering edge cases like how different file formats might structure their questions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":38880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":927},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c637cc40-8152-404a-aa5d-36736366ea90","uuid":"c8122792-c5de-4a6a-b368-fb9eaaa3cb32"}
