{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Aq8FLkirJcBfe7waAnu5ei","type":"tool_result","content":"60\t---\n61\t\n62\t## 第三部分：简答题（5 题，每题 6 分，共 30 分）\n63\t\n64\t26. 列出良好咨询区域的六大特征，并说明每项的具体标准。\n65\t27. 简述中医四诊（望、闻、问、切）的内容与意义。\n66\t28. 区分\"适应症\"、\"注意事项\"与\"禁忌症\"，并各举两例。\n67\t29. 阐述完整的转介流程（≥ 7 个步骤）。\n68\t30. 写出推拿服务方案应包含的至少 8 项要素。\n69\t\n70\t---\n71\t\n72\t## 第四部分：综合案例题（共 20 分）\n73\t\n74\t**案例：**\n75\t张女士，48 岁，华裔，文员，主诉\"左肩疼痛 2 个月伴左上肢麻木\"。她服用降压药 (Amlodipine) 5 年，最近自测血压 140/95 mmHg。无骨折史，无皮肤问题。已签署同意书。\n76\t\n77\t请回答：\n78\t\n79\t(a) 此案例中应特别留意的注意事项有哪些？（5 分）\n80\t(b) 你将进行哪些四诊评估？请逐一说明。（5 分）\n81\t(c) 应选择何种推拿模式，并说明理由。（5 分）\n82\t(d) 写出此客户的推拿方案要点（至少 6 项）。（5 分）\n83\t\n84\t---\n85\t\n86\t## 答案要点（导师参考）\n87\t\n88\t| 题号 | 答案 |\n89\t|------|------|\n90\t| 1 | 私密性 |\n91\t| 2 | 身份证 |\n92\t| 3 | 安全 |\n93\t| 4 | 切 |\n94\t| 5 | Tóu bù |\n95\t| 6 | 紧张 |\n96\t| 7 | 开放性 |\n97\t| 8 | 小儿 |\n98\t| 9 | 2013 |\n99\t| 10 | 999 |\n100\t| 11–25 | B, B, C, C, C, C, B, B, B, C, C, B, B, B, B |\n101\t| 26 | 氛围（柔和音乐）、温度（22–25°C）、噪音（< 50 dB）、灯光（暖色柔和）、私密性（屏风/单独室）、安全（防滑、急救箱、灭火器） |\n102\t| 27 | 望（神色形态）、闻（声/气）、问（十问）、切（脉/触诊）；意义：综合判断病机与体质 |\n103\t| 28 | 适应症：肌肉酸痛、失眠；注意：饭后、孕妇；禁忌：出血、骨折 |\n104\t| 29 | 识别 → 解释必要性 → 取得同意 → 填写转介表 → 推荐机构 → 客户记录登记 → 追踪结果 |\n105\t| 30 | 资料、主诉、适应症、禁忌排除、模式、部位手法、时长频率、注意事项、自我护理、复诊、评估指标 |\n106\t| 案例 (a) | 高血压控制不佳、降压药、年龄、长期文员姿势 |\n107\t| 案例 (b) | 望（肩高低、面色）、闻（呼吸）、问（十问 + 用药 + 血压）、切（颈肩张力 + 脉象） |\n108\t| 案例 (c) | 肌骨推拿；针对肩颈麻木 + 文员职业病 |\n109\t| 案例 (d) | 模式肌骨推拿 / 部位颈肩 / 揉按拿手法 / 60min × 6 次 / 力度温和（高血压） / 疗后避风 / 监测 VAS / 调整工作姿势 / 1 周后复诊 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c637cc40-8152-404a-aa5d-36736366ea90","uuid":"1406aa67-4dc4-4037-a63f-7fa7a79d13d4","timestamp":"2026-04-17T09:34:12.491Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/noss-to-wim/tuinalogy-services/C01/KA.md","content":"---\n\n## 第三部分：简答题（5 题，每题 6 分，共 30 分）\n\n26. 列出良好咨询区域的六大特征，并说明每项的具体标准。\n27. 简述中医四诊（望、闻、问、切）的内容与意义。\n28. 区分\"适应症\"、\"注意事项\"与\"禁忌症\"，并各举两例。\n29. 阐述完整的转介流程（≥ 7 个步骤）。\n30. 写出推拿服务方案应包含的至少 8 项要素。\n\n---\n\n## 第四部分：综合案例题（共 20 分）\n\n**案例：**\n张女士，48 岁，华裔，文员，主诉\"左肩疼痛 2 个月伴左上肢麻木\"。她服用降压药 (Amlodipine) 5 年，最近自测血压 140/95 mmHg。无骨折史，无皮肤问题。已签署同意书。\n\n请回答：\n\n(a) 此案例中应特别留意的注意事项有哪些？（5 分）\n(b) 你将进行哪些四诊评估？请逐一说明。（5 分）\n(c) 应选择何种推拿模式，并说明理由。（5 分）\n(d) 写出此客户的推拿方案要点（至少 6 项）。（5 分）\n\n---\n\n## 答案要点（导师参考）\n\n| 题号 | 答案 |\n|------|------|\n| 1 | 私密性 |\n| 2 | 身份证 |\n| 3 | 安全 |\n| 4 | 切 |\n| 5 | Tóu bù |\n| 6 | 紧张 |\n| 7 | 开放性 |\n| 8 | 小儿 |\n| 9 | 2013 |\n| 10 | 999 |\n| 11–25 | B, B, C, C, C, C, B, B, B, C, C, B, B, B, B |\n| 26 | 氛围（柔和音乐）、温度（22–25°C）、噪音（< 50 dB）、灯光（暖色柔和）、私密性（屏风/单独室）、安全（防滑、急救箱、灭火器） |\n| 27 | 望（神色形态）、闻（声/气）、问（十问）、切（脉/触诊）；意义：综合判断病机与体质 |\n| 28 | 适应症：肌肉酸痛、失眠；注意：饭后、孕妇；禁忌：出血、骨折 |\n| 29 | 识别 → 解释必要性 → 取得同意 → 填写转介表 → 推荐机构 → 客户记录登记 → 追踪结果 |\n| 30 | 资料、主诉、适应症、禁忌排除、模式、部位手法、时长频率、注意事项、自我护理、复诊、评估指标 |\n| 案例 (a) | 高血压控制不佳、降压药、年龄、长期文员姿势 |\n| 案例 (b) | 望（肩高低、面色）、闻（呼吸）、问（十问 + 用药 + 血压）、切（颈肩张力 + 脉象） |\n| 案例 (c) | 肌骨推拿；针对肩颈麻木 + 文员职业病 |\n| 案例 (d) | 模式肌骨推拿 / 部位颈肩 / 揉按拿手法 / 60min × 6 次 / 力度温和（高血压） / 疗后避风 / 监测 VAS / 调整工作姿势 / 1 周后复诊 |","numLines":50,"startLine":60,"totalLines":131}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01V5G2UagaFzN3NNufJpybLB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. The tuinalogy KA files use a different format:\n- Section 1: 填空题 (Fill in the blank) — numbered 1-10\n- Section 2: 选择题 (MCQ) — numbered 11-25\n- Section 3: 简答题 (Short answer) — numbered 26-30\n- Section 4: 综合案例题 (Case study/Scenario) — not individually numbered but has sub-parts (a), (b), (c), (d)\n\nFor question type detection in Chinese format:\n- 填空题 → short_answer (~ 2-3 min, similar to MCQ)\n\n\n- 选择题 → mcq (2 min each)\n- 简答题 → short_answer (6 min each)\n- 综合案例题 / 案例题 → scenario (8-10 min)\n\nI need to handle both English section headers like Section A/B/C and Chinese ones like 第X部分. For MCQ detection, I'll look for the English pattern `**A\\d+.**` within Section A or lines with option markers like `- A.` / `- B.`, and for Chinese I'll count numbered lines in the 选择题 section.\n\nActually, I think the cleaner approach is to just look for question number patterns and count them by section type. I'm writing a function that reads the assessment file and counts each question type—for practical assessments it looks for TASK headers, and for other files it counts MCQs, short answers, and scenario questions using regex patterns to identify the question formats.\n\nStill writing the question detection logic... I'm realizing the classification issue — 填空题 (fill-in-the-blank) doesn't fit neatly into the acceptance criteria, which only specifies multiple choice, essay, scenario, and practical tasks. Since fill-in-the-blank items are quick to complete, I'll treat them as multiple choice equivalents at 2 minutes each, rather than introducing a new category that isn't in the requirements. Looking at the test structure, I'm calculating the time allocation for each section. The fill-in-the-blank and multiple choice questions both take 2 minutes each, so that's 20 and 30 minutes respectively. The short answer questions need 30 minutes total at 6 minutes per question. For the case study with 4 sub-questions, I'm reconsidering whether 9 minutes is enough—since it's worth 20 marks total, I should probably allocate more time, maybe treating each sub-question as needing closer to 5-6 minutes rather than lumping it as a single 9-minute task. Writing regex pattern...\n\nFor section 4, the sub-questions labeled (a) through (d) should each count as a scenario item. I'm checking if each line matches that pattern and incrementing the scenario count accordingly. Then I can calculate the total time: 25 MCQ questions at 2 minutes each gives 50 minutes, 5 short answer questions at 6 minutes each gives 30 minutes, and 4 scenario sub-questions at 9 minutes each gives 36 minutes, totaling 116 minutes against the time limit.\n\nLooking at the actual assessment duration in the file, it specifies 120 minutes for the written portion plus 30 minutes for review, so 116 minutes is quite close to that stated time. However, the WIM KA limit should be 60 minutes, which means this assessment is running at 193% of the expected limit — so the flagging is working correctly to identify that this KA is significantly over capacity.\n\nNow I'm examining the PA structure for the tuinalogy assessment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1471,"cache_read_input_tokens":47934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1471},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c637cc40-8152-404a-aa5d-36736366ea90","uuid":"7702ccba-ff6e-4149-bdf3-5c65759e9dbc"}
